description:
PROBLEM
`rookery/0.2.0` ships a `.marrow.typ` — 312 lines that mint one page per note, build the note-backlinks and page-backlinks maps, and apply the projects `idea-page-template` — and NOTHING in this repo exercises any of it. `demo/pure/` is native `typst compile` only, and its own `root.typ` says so: no rheo, one compilation unit, in-page fragments rather than cross-page hrefs. So every rheo-only path is verified today only by hand against the sibling `rookery.ohrg.org` repo.

Untested in-repo as a result: `.marrow.typ` end to end, `_note-href`/`_page-href` depth arithmetic on a NESTED vertebra (the case a root-only spine cannot catch), `_page-links` bracket-depth counting, `_is-vertebra` filtering minted pages out of page backlinks (its comment records six wrong backlinks when that filter was missing), `idea-page-template`, `minted-depth = window-depth + 1`, and the minted-page References block.

STEPS
1. Add `rookery/0.2.0/demo/rheo/` with a `rheo.toml`, following the shape `blogfeed/0.1.1/demo/` and `tooltip/0.1.0/demo/` already use.
2. Make the spine deliberately awkward, so the arithmetic is actually under test:
   - a root `index.typ`;
   - at least one NESTED vertebra (handle `sub:page`), so `../` prefixing is non-trivial;
   - notes windowed ACROSS vertebrae in both directions, so mutual transclusion is exercised (this is the configuration `_ideas-outline-data`s `window-depth` guard was measured against);
   - a note whose body contains a nested `#idea` and a nested `#window`;
   - a page-level link written in ordinary prose OUTSIDE any note, which is the only thing that produces a page backlink;
   - a `#show: rookery.with(idea-page-template: ..)` naming a top-level function (lib.typ:296 warns an inline closure per vertebra breaks `.final()`);
   - a configured `bibliography:` with citations both in prose and inside notes.
3. Add a `Justfile` beside it with `build:`/`watch:` recipes calling `rheo compile`/`rheo watch`, mirroring `demo/pure/Justfile`.
4. Assert on the OUTPUT, not just that it compiles — a grep-based check is enough and needs no new tooling: that `ideas/<slug>.html` exists per note, that a nested vertebras hrefs carry the right number of `../`, that a minted page carries a Context section and a Backlinks section, and that no minted page appears in another notes page-backlinks list.
5. Wire it into the CI check workflow (see that bead) once rheo is installable there. If it is not, say so in the Justfile and keep the demo runnable locally — a demo nobody can run is worse than none.

NON-GOALS
Replacing `demo/pure`. It exists to prove the package works as a plain Typst package with no rheo, which is half the packages contract (readme, "Two modes").

VERIFY
`cd rookery/0.2.0/demo/rheo && just build` produces the minted pages and the assertion script passes.
